# Response headers for the dashboard's own files.
#
# A page that can be framed can be overlaid: an attacker puts a transparent
# copy of the page over it and captures the click on "Sign in with GitHub".
# frame-ancestors in a <meta> tag does nothing - the browser ignores it
# there - so the refusal has to come from a header. X-Frame-Options is the
# older spelling of the same rule, kept for browsers that only know it.
#
# The Worker's API answers carry their own hardening headers; this file is
# for the static assets it serves (Cloudflare Workers `_headers` format).
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
